    "report": "The notice of a new message now carries `listingId`, and the work is committed on `main` as `32a669a`. I did not push. Unit tests (1049), the full e2e run (607), typecheck, lint, format and `check:conventions` all pass.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging:** `MessageSentEvent` now records the conversation's `listingId`, set at both places it is recorded (start and send). `MessageSentHandler` passes it on.\n- **Shared kernel:** `MessageSentPayload` gains `listingId`. This is the contract between Messaging and Notifications, so it is the one place the new field crosses contexts.\n- **Notifications:** `MessageNoticeBody` gets `listingId`, the owing rule and the event handler pass it through, and `PostgresNotices` stores it in the existing `listing_id` column and reads it back. Reading it back matters because an un-accepted notice is re-sent from the database, and it must keep the same body.\n- **Specs:** fixtures and body expectations updated, and the message-notice e2e spec now asserts `listingId` on the offered notice.\n\n**Decisions I made**\n- I stored `listingId` in the existing `listing_id` column rather than adding a migration. No schema change was needed.\n- I put the field on the integration event itself rather than having Notifications look up the conversation. A lookup would be a new cross-context link that would need a declared relationship.\n\n**Gap to decide on**\n- Notices already owed but not yet accepted when this ships have no stored listing id, so they will be re-sent with `listingId: null`. The column is nullable, and the body type says `string`, so the type does not catch it. Fixing it needs a backfill from Messaging's data, and Notifications cannot do that without a cross-context read. Options are a one-off backfill owned by Messaging, or accepting the null for those legacy notices. I did not pick one.\n\n**Other notes**\n- The request said to commit on the current branch, so I committed on `main` as asked, not on a new branch.\n- The first unit run had one failure, which was my own missed fixture, and I fixed it. I also confirmed the clean tree passes before my change.\n- `MessageNoticeOwing.owe` still defaults `at` to `new Date()`. The project guide says time parameters should always be passed in, but this request does not touch time, so I left it alone.",
